  "term": "Schedule for Affective Disorders and Schizophrenia",
  "definition": "The Schedule for Affective Disorders and Schizophrenia is a semi-structured psychiatric interview used to assess and diagnose a wide range of current and past mental health problems. In its child and adolescent present-and-lifetime form, it is used for ages roughly 6 to 18 and has versions adapted to DSM categories.",
